From d458e8d96edf3b4b662c8fcf46fcbc52e2c14ba1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:06:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] fix(app): place finished workspaces at the last prompt
 sent there

The sidebar showed, sorted and grouped finished workspaces by when they entered the done
bucket. Every time an app connects, the daemon reopens closed chats to read their history,
and that reopening restamps the time, so workspaces untouched for days showed as just used.
On one host, 75 of 170 chats sat hours or weeks after their last prompt.

A finished workspace now uses the last prompt sent there, which only moves when you send one,
and falls back to the done entry time when it never got a prompt. Running and attention rows
keep their bucket entry time. Command Center ranks workspaces by the same time.
